    "probe_text": "I now have the full picture. Here is the complete, ordered list.\n\n## POST /api/owners \u2014 validations & side-effects, in execution order\n\nEverything below runs inside a single transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]` on every step), so all DB writes commit once at the end.\n\n**0. Authorization (gate, before any step)**\n- `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"` \u2014 caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN` or the request is denied.\n\n**1. `ValidateOwnerFields`** \u2014 *(reads the `@RequestBody` here, once)*\n- Validation: `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-null and non-blank; `address` must be non-blank *after normalization*. All offending fields are collected and reported together \u2192 **400** (`OwnerFieldsInvalidException`).\n- Side-effect: normalizes `address` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE) and writes it back.\n- Validation + side-effect: normalizes `telephone` to E.164 (keeps `+`/country code, else assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`); invalid \u2192 **400**; valid normalized value written back.\n- Validation + side-effect: if `email` is present it must be syntactically valid \u2192 else **400**; otherwise lower-cased and written back.\n- Publishes the normalized body for later steps.\n\n**2. `ValidatePostcode`**\n- Validation only (no mutation): if `postcode` present it must be exactly 4 digits; and if the city maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW 2000\u20132099, Melbourne\u2192VIC 3000\u20133099, Brisbane\u2192QLD 4000\u20134099) it must fall in range. Malformed/out-of-range \u2192 **400**. Absent postcode is accepted; unknown city accepts any 4-digit code.\n\n**3. `CheckOwnerCityCapacity`**\n- Validation: rejects with **409** (`OwnerCityCapacityConflictException`) if the owner's city (case-insensitive) already holds \u2265 50 owners.\n\n**4. `CheckOwnerDailyCreateLimit`**\n- Validation: rejects with **429** (`OwnerDailyCreateLimitException`) if \u2265 100 owners already have a `registrationDate` equal to today's *business day* (weekends rolled forward).\n\n**5. `BuildOwner`**\n- Side-effect: maps the DTO to an `Owner` entity; defaults `registrationDate` to today if unset; rolls the registration date forward off weekends to the next business day.\n\n**6. `AssignHouseholdId`** \u2014 *(only when body has `sharesHousehold: true`)*\n- Side-effect: derives a stable 12-char hex `householdId` from normalized last name + address; sets it on the new owner **and back-fills + saves it onto existing same-lastName/same-address owners** (a write before the main save).\n\n**7. `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`**\n- Validation: builds `identityKey = normalizedTelephone|email|householdId` and rejects with **409** (`OwnerIdentityConflictException`) if it exactly matches any existing owner's key. (Runs after household assignment so the id is in the key, and before save so it isn't compared to itself.)\n\n**8. `AssignHouseholdMemberCount`**\n- Side-effect: sets `householdMemberCount` = existing owners sharing the `householdId` + 1 (the new owner); 1 when no household.\n\n**9. `AssignNamesakeCount`**\n- Side-effect: sets `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive), excluding this owner.\n\n**10. `AssignCustomerCode`**\n- Side-effect: sets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where NNNN is a per-city sequence = (owners already in that city) + 1.\n\n**11. `AssignBulkSignupWarning`**\n- Side-effect: sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` when > 80 owners were already created today (same business-day basis as step 4).\n\n**12. `SaveOwner`**\n- Side-effect: persists the new owner (generating its id).\n\n**13. `AuditOwnerCreated`**\n- Side-effect: emits an `AUDIT` log line with the owner id, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and derived `membershipLevel` (after save so the id exists).\n\n**14. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`**\n- Side-effect: maps to `OwnerDto` and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nNote two DB-write side-effects occur before the main save: the household back-fill in step 6 and the save in step 12 \u2014 both within the one transaction, so they commit together (or roll back together if a later step throws)."
